{{Documentation}}
This template is a profile template used for displaying [[Meow Medals]] similarly to the in-game screen. The medals are arranged in pages containing 20 medals each, requiring vertical scrolling to view other pages. Hovering over an image of a meow medal shows its name.

==Parameters==
<pre>
{{MedalList|Medal Name 1|Medal Name 2|Medal Name 3| ... |partial = number 1, number 2, number3, ...}}
</pre>
The listed medal names should be typed without stars and with accurate spelling and capitalization. The meow medals with these names will be shown as unlocked and counted to show the number of unlocked meow medals at the upper right corner of the template.

The optional parameter <code>partial</code> is for displaying meow medals that have been partially revealed (only the rarity). This takes a list of numbers that tell the position of each medal that is partially revealed. The position of a medal is determined by counting horizontally from top to bottom and left to right, starting at the top left corner on each page. For example, the medal on page 2 in the 1st row and 3rd column has position 23. List the positions separated by commas and optional spaces, but do not include any characters other than numbers, commas, and spaces.

In the case where a medal is included in <code>partial</code> while being passed as a normal argument, the medal shows as unlocked. All medals that are not named in the arguments remain unknown.

